4139534643 true] [17592186300843 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/assets/e9e4c56d6dbedb8d1a185c58bc2f9c8c02d333b2532e3f45e8304185b5982908.png" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534643 true] [17592186300843 1111 #uuid "d726ad90-cb2a-5435-9175-cc144326c701" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300844 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/assets/51ac4ad5bbc626c58ddbb6efd8c06bb665ef0849591dd846dd959756ea6e41b6.png" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534643 true] [17592186300844 1111 #uuid "86d8467f-614e-5f2c-95ce-c7c3074a659f" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300845 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300846 13194139534643 true] [17592186300845 1089 "q-216703" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300845 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534643 true] [17592186300845 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/assets/91eb6ed60e58b03732bdcea3e9858db452d2d998c6a6abed538bbcc76412ed4c.png)\n\nFind the $9$th root of unity highlighted in the diagram above." 13194139534643 true] [17592186300845 1113 #uuid "f52d2e5e-410c-538e-83f2-0b54c29688e7" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300845 1145 "The $n$th roots of unity lie at the vertices of a regular $n$-gon inscribed inside the unit circle in the complex plane. One of the vertices of this regular $n$-gon must lie at the point $(1,0).$\n\nFirst, we express the complex number $1$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta }.$ Notice that $|1|=1$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(1)=0.$ Hence, \n\n$$\n1={e}^{\\text{i}(0+2k\\pi )}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is an integer. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{9}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}}\\,⟹\\,z=({e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}})^{1/9}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}/9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the index $k$ of our root of unity, we enumerate the roots in the diagram counter-clockwise, starting with the root at $(1,0)$ corresponding to $k=0,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/assets/9b3977b8b51c54a1ef552cff48a3be5a269c92a96742cba5c87e618bb616e5a0.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the required root corresponds to $k=7.$ Substituting this into the expression for roots, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}_{7}={e}^{2(7)\\pi \\text{i}/9}={e}^{14\\pi \\text{i}/9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300846 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300847 13194139534643 true] [17592186300846 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300848 13194139534643 true] [17592186300846 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300849 13194139534643 true] [17592186300846 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300850 13194139534643 true] [17592186300846 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300851 13194139534643 true] [17592186300846 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534643 true] [17592186300846 1041 "selection" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300846 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300848 13194139534643 true] [17592186300846 1110 #uuid "8ff19d2a-38c0-55de-b798-c587f76a0f09" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300847 1034 "{e}^{11\\pi \\text{i}/6}" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534643 true] [17592186300847 1111 #uuid "d06b409b-4fef-5c88-b3e5-293325ee33d8" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300848 1034 "{e}^{14\\pi \\text{i}/9}" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300848 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534643 true] [17592186300848 1111 #uuid "59f526c2-f262-5e1b-81d7-b6e3065ce0e1" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300849 1034 "{e}^{12\\pi \\text{i}/9}" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300849 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534643 true] [17592186300849 1111 #uuid "f3b82cb2-d5ea-5632-91f7-cc8406391289" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300850 1034 "{e}^{16\\pi \\text{i}/9}" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534643 true] [17592186300850 1111 #uuid "2abddbcc-885f-500f-a58f-c73a3955f1d8" 13194139534643 true] [17592186300851 1034 "{e}^{5\\p